; claude: the text editors, as Tui.program values (plan_terminal.md,
; section 6): Tui_vi (vi, 1976: modes, and commands as a language of
; operators and motions, over lines) and Tui_emacs (Emacs, 1985: a
; Lisp machine with a screen), over Gap_buffer (Emacs's text, a hole
; where the editing happens), Emacs_editor (the core: buffers, undo
; list, kill ring, the primitives given to Lisp) and Emacs_simple (the
; commands, in Lisp, over libs/languages/lisp); and Tui_turbo (Turbo
; Pascal's IDE, 1992: menus, dialogs and a blue window drawn with the
; PC's box characters, over libs/languages/pascal). Run on the
; playground by the Textmode way (apps/devtools' TinyVi, TinyEmacs,
; TinyTurboPascal) and in a real terminal by Tty_unix
; (apps/devtools/tty/).
;
; Pure OCaml, no playground: a private library, installed as part of
; elm_playground.
(library
 (name appkit_editor)
 (package elm_playground)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries terminal lisp pascal)
)
